## Database Dump & Restore (localhost)

Rendered into `DB_DUMP.md` (gitignored - contains real secrets, never commit it). Run every command from the repo root.

### 1. Render this template (Windows: Git Bash/WSL, mac: any shell)

```bash
infisical run --env=dev --recursive -c "envsubst < .deployment/localhost/DB_DUMP.template > .deployment/localhost/DB_DUMP.md"
```

### 2. Install 7-Zip (once per machine)

- macOS: `brew install sevenzip` (command: `7zz`)
- Windows: `winget install 7zip.7zip` (command: `C:\Program Files\7-Zip\7z.exe`, not on PATH by default)

### 3. Dump & restore

Scripts live in `.deployment/localhost/scripts/` (`.sh` for macOS, `.ps1` for Windows) and can be run from any directory. Archives land in `.deployment/localhost/dump/` as
timestamped `.7z` files; each dump deletes the previous one, so only the latest is kept. Commit the `.7z` files; the uncompressed `.sql` is gitignored.

Plain SQL dump (`pg_dump -Fp --clean --if-exists`), restored with `psql`.

#### macOS (zsh/bash)

```bash
bash .deployment/localhost/scripts/db-dump.sh ${DB_USER} ${DB_DATABASE}
```

```bash
bash .deployment/localhost/scripts/db-restore.sh ${DB_USER} ${DB_DATABASE}
```

#### Windows (PowerShell)

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .deployment\localhost\scripts\db-dump.ps1 ${DB_USER} ${DB_DATABASE}
```

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .deployment\localhost\scripts\db-restore.ps1 ${DB_USER} ${DB_DATABASE}
```
